    "body": "# User description\nFinal ramp step (5→25→**100**), criteria-gated rather than calendar-gated per Joshua's pace directive: move at maximum safe speed when the pause buys no new evidence.\n\n**Evidence:** zero errors in either cohort across every probe since the first deploy (24h+ at 5%; re-verified at 25% today — 160 reqs/80 buckets at deploy + periodic probes since). Cohort latency parity-or-better for cards at every check; latest probe: cards p50 101ms / p95 237ms vs legacy p50 104ms / p95 391ms. Split tracking nominal at both steps. Backfill delta-0; sync verified writing; drift fallback active.\n\n**At 100%:** DB load profile improves (small indexed card reads replace 45KB location docs + images N+1). Watch through the next traffic peak: cards responseTimeInMs p95/p99 in morgan logs, 5xx flat, drift warns ~0. **Rollback unchanged and instant: `CARDS_ROLLOUT_PCT=0` + redeploy** (or 25 to step back down).\n\nOne-line diff: `CARDS_ROLLOUT_PCT=25` → `100` in `infra/prod.env`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n\n# Generated description\nRaise the <code>cards</code> read-model rollout in <code>infra/prod.env</code> from 25% to 100% so production traffic fully uses the new card read path. Keep the existing <code>TILE_READ_MODEL</code>, telemetry, cache, and image-attachment flags in place to support the cards flow.\n\n\n<details><summary>Latest Contributors(0)</summary><table><tr><th>User</th><th>Commit</th><th>Date</th></tr></table></details>\n<sub><a href=\"https://baz.co/changes/stepscode/atly-tileserver/350?tool=ast\">Review this PR on Baz</a> | <a href=\"https://baz.co/agents/baz\">Customize your next review</a></sub>",
